Backport python-tcod's modern SDL header parser compatibility exclusions.

Source: https://github.com/libtcod/python-tcod/blob/19.6.3/build_sdl.py
New SDL2 headers put whitespace between ')' and ';'.  The old parser therefore
failed to exclude va_list declarations, whose platform-specific ABI CFFI
cannot describe.  This retains the upstream policy of excluding only these
uncallable va_list entry points, not ordinary SDL functions or game behavior.

Also backport the upstream IGNORE_DEFINES additions: compiler annotations and
platform configuration flags are not exported SDL integer constants, while
SDL_FLT_EPSILON is floating-point.  This fixes CFFI classification, preserving
all ordinary callable SDL/audio APIs without suppressing compiler diagnostics.

--- a/build_sdl.py
+++ b/build_sdl.py
@@ -31 +31 @@
-RE_VAFUNC = re.compile(r"^.*?\([^()]*va_list[^()]*\);$", re.MULTILINE)
+RE_VAFUNC = re.compile(r"^.*?\([^()]*va_list[^()]*\)\s*;\s*$", re.MULTILINE)
@@ -57,0 +58,6 @@
+        "SDL_HAS_FALLTHROUGH",
+        "SDL_NO_THREAD_SAFETY_ANALYSIS",
+        "SDL_SCOPED_CAPABILITY",
+        "SDL_NODISCARD",
+        "SDL_NOLONGLONG",
+        "SDL_WINAPI_FAMILY_PHONE",
@@ -65,0 +72,6 @@
+        # Ignore floating point symbols.
+        "SDL_FLT_EPSILON",
+        # Conditional config flags which might be missing.
+        "SDL_VIDEO_RENDER_D3D12",
+        "SDL_SENSOR_WINDOWS",
+        "SDL_SENSOR_DUMMY",
